# TypeScript/JavaScript (Node.js) coding style

Narrows `core-common-rules`' style rules to Node.js server, library and CLI
code in TypeScript or JavaScript. Applies to `*.ts`/`*.js`/`*.mjs`/`*.cjs`;
JSX/TSX component code belongs to the `react` pack, which extends this one.

## Typing and module shape

- Keep `tsconfig.json`'s `strict: true` on; do not narrow it or add per-file `// @ts-nocheck`.
- Prefer `unknown` over `any` for a value of unknown shape (parsed JSON, a fetch body); narrow with a type guard before use.
- Match the project's declared `moduleResolution` (`nodenext` or `bundler`); do not mix `require()` and `import` in code run as ESM (`"type": "module"`).
- Import Node built-ins with the `node:` prefix (`node:fs`, `node:path`, `node:crypto`).
- Use `import type { X } from "..."` (or `verbatimModuleSyntax` when the project enables it) for type-only imports.

## Naming and structure

- One cohesive export group per module; split a file mixing unrelated public exports along the seam its imports show.
- Prefer named exports over a single default export in a module with more than one thing to export.

## Async and errors

- `async`/`await` over raw `.then()` in new code; a `.then()` chain longer than one link becomes `await` with `try`/`catch`.
- Await every `Promise`, return it to a caller that awaits it, or discard it explicitly with `void somePromise()`; never a bare unreferenced promise statement.
- Pass `AbortSignal` (`AbortSignal.timeout(ms)` or a caller `signal`) into `fetch` and other cancelable APIs instead of `setTimeout` + `Promise.race`.
- Throw `Error` (or a subclass) whose message names what failed and the relevant value; chain the cause with `new Error("...", { cause })`.
- Never catch an error only to `console.log` and continue as if it succeeded; rethrow, return a typed failure, or handle it.

## Imports and formatting

- Format and lint with the project's configured tool (`eslint`, `prettier`, `biome`); do not introduce a second formatter.
- Group imports Node built-ins, third-party, local (relative), one blank line between; run `eslint-plugin-import`/`simple-import-sort` when configured.
- Use explicit `.js` extensions on relative ESM imports when `moduleResolution: nodenext` requires them; match the surrounding files.
